  "rationale": "The eight mask handlers applied any mapped mask change to the held steps when a sequencer step was held, whichever channel the map named. A fixed channel-2 map therefore wrote channel 2's held-step masks from the selected channel's on-screen value (channel 1 velocity 50 made channel 2 step 2 read 53), and those edits bypassed memory, whose held-step commits are keyed to the selected channel. Arbitrated SEM-017 (fixed-map-ignores-held-steps): the held-step branch applies only when the handled channel is the selected channel.",
  "oracle": "README MIDI Controller Mapping (203): channel parameters control a parameter of a specific channel regardless of which channel is selected.",
